        <scope doc="When replacing one block of lines with another, search the blocksfor *similar* lines; the best-matching pair (if any) is used as a synch point, and intraline difference marking is done on the similar pair. Lots of work, but often worth it.  Example:  &gt;&gt;&gt; d = Differ() &gt;&gt;&gt; results = d._fancy_replace(['abcDefghiJkl\n'], 0, 1, ...                            ['abcdefGhijkl\n'], 0, 1) &gt;&gt;&gt; print(''.join(results), end=&quot;&quot;)" ilk="function" line="948" lineend="1044" name="_fancy_replace" signature="Differ() -&gt; When replacing one block of lines with another, search the blocksfor *similar* lines; the best-matching pair (if any) is used as a synch point, and intraline difference marking is done on the similar pair. Lots of work, but often worth it.  Example:  &gt;&gt;&gt; d">
