    <scope doc="fixdiv - tool to fix division operators.&#10;To use this tool, first run `python -Qwarnall yourscript.py 2&gt;warnings'. This runs the script `yourscript.py' while writing warning messages about all uses of the classic division operator to the file `warnings'.  The warnings look like this:  &lt;file&gt;:&lt;line&gt;: DeprecationWarning: classic &lt;type&gt; division  The warnings are written to stderr, so you must use `2&gt;' for the I/O redirect.  I know of no way to redirect stderr on Windows in a DOS box, so you will have to modify the script to set sys.stderr to some" ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Tools.Scripts.fixdiv">
