    <scope doc="Word completion for GNU readline.&#10;The completer completes keywords, built-ins and globals in a selectable namespace (which defaults to __main__); when completing NAME.NAME..., it evaluates (!) the expression up to the last dot and completes its attributes.  It's very cool to do &quot;import sys&quot; type &quot;sys.&quot;, hit the completion key (twice), and see the list of names defined by the sys module!  Tip: to use the tab key as the completion key, call  readline.parse_and_bind(&quot;tab: complete&quot;)" ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Lib.rlcompleter">
