    <scope doc="This module provides primitive operations to write multi-threaded programs.The 'threading' module provides a more convenient interface." ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="_thread">
      <scope classrefs="object" doc="A lock object is a synchronization primitive.  To create a lock,call the PyThread_allocate_lock() function.  Methods are:  acquire() -- lock the lock, possibly blocking until it can be obtained release() -- unlock of the lock locked() -- test whether the lock is currently locked  A lock is not owned by the thread that locked it; another thread may unlock it.  A thread attempting to lock a lock that it has already locked will block until another thread unlocks it.  Deadlocks may ensue." ilk="class" name="LockType">
        <scope doc="acquire([wait]) -&gt; None or bool(acquire_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Lock the lock.  Without argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked (even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release the lock, and return None once the lock is acquired. With an argument, this will only block if the argument is true, and the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired. The blocking operation is interruptible." ilk="function" name="acquire" signature="acquire([wait]) -&gt; None or bool(acquire_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Lock the lock.  Without argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked (even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release the lock, and return None once the lock is acquired. With an argument, this will only block if the argument is true, and the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired. The blocking operation is interruptible." />
        <scope doc="release()(release_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state, but it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it." ilk="function" name="release" signature="release()(release_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state, but it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it." />
        <scope doc="acquire([wait]) -&gt; None or bool(acquire_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Lock the lock.  Without argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked (even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release the lock, and return None once the lock is acquired. With an argument, this will only block if the argument is true, and the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired. The blocking operation is interruptible." ilk="function" name="acquire_lock" signature="acquire([wait]) -&gt; None or bool(acquire_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Lock the lock.  Without argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked (even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release the lock, and return None once the lock is acquired. With an argument, this will only block if the argument is true, and the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired. The blocking operation is interruptible." />
        <scope doc="release()(release_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state, but it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it." ilk="function" name="release_lock" signature="release()(release_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state, but it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it." />
        <scope doc="release()(release_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state, but it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it." ilk="function" name="__exit__" signature="release()(release_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked waiting for the lock to acquire the lock.  The lock must be in the locked state, but it needn't be locked by the same thread that unlocks it." />
        <scope doc="acquire([wait]) -&gt; None or bool(acquire_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Lock the lock.  Without argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked (even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release the lock, and return None once the lock is acquired. With an argument, this will only block if the argument is true, and the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired. The blocking operation is interruptible." ilk="function" name="__enter__" signature="acquire([wait]) -&gt; None or bool(acquire_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Lock the lock.  Without argument, this blocks if the lock is already locked (even by the same thread), waiting for another thread to release the lock, and return None once the lock is acquired. With an argument, this will only block if the argument is true, and the return value reflects whether the lock is acquired. The blocking operation is interruptible." />
        <scope doc="locked() -&gt; bool(locked_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Return whether the lock is in the locked state." ilk="function" name="locked" returns="bool" signature="locked() -&gt; bool(locked_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Return whether the lock is in the locked state." />
        <scope doc="locked() -&gt; bool(locked_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Return whether the lock is in the locked state." ilk="function" name="locked_lock" returns="bool" signature="locked() -&gt; bool(locked_lock() is an obsolete synonym)  Return whether the lock is in the locked state." />
      </scope>
      <scope classrefs="object" doc="&#10;" ilk="class" name="RLock">
        <scope doc="Lock the lock. `blocking` indicates whether we should wait&#10;for the lock to be available or not." ilk="function" name="acquire" returns="bool" signature="acquire(blocking=True) -&gt; bool" />
        <scope doc="Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked&#10;waiting for the lock to acquire the lock. The lock must be&#10;in the locked state, and must be locked by the same thread&#10;that unlocks it; otherwise a `RuntimeError` is raised." ilk="function" name="release" signature="release()" />
        <scope doc="Release the lock, allowing another thread that is blocked&#10;waiting for the lock to acquire the lock. The lock must be&#10;in the locked state, and must be locked by the same thread&#10;that unlocks it; otherwise a `RuntimeError` is raised." ilk="function" name="__exit__" signature="release()" />
        <scope doc="For internal use by `threading.Condition`." ilk="function" name="_acquire_restore" signature="_acquire_restore(state) -&gt; None" />
        <scope doc="Lock the lock. `blocking` indicates whether we should wait&#10;for the lock to be available or not." ilk="function" name="__enter__" returns="bool" signature="acquire(blocking=True) -&gt; bool" />
