      <scope doc="start_new_thread(function, args[, kwargs])(start_new() is an obsolete synonym)  Start a new thread and return its identifier.  The thread will call the function with positional arguments from the tuple args and keyword arguments taken from the optional dictionary kwargs.  The thread exits when the function returns; the return value is ignored.  The thread will also exit when the function raises an unhandled exception; a stack trace will be printed unless the exception is SystemExit." ilk="function" name="start_new" signature="start_new_thread(function, args[, kwargs])(start_new() is an obsolete synonym)  Start a new thread and return its identifier.  The thread will call the function with positional arguments from the tuple args and keyword arguments taken from the optional dictionary kwargs.  The thread exits when the function returns; the return value is ignored.  The thread will also exit when the function raises an unhandled exception; a stack trace will be printed unless the exception is SystemExit." />
      <scope doc="start_new_thread(function, args[, kwargs])(start_new() is an obsolete synonym)  Start a new thread and return its identifier.  The thread will call the function with positional arguments from the tuple args and keyword arguments taken from the optional dictionary kwargs.  The thread exits when the function returns; the return value is ignored.  The thread will also exit when the function raises an unhandled exception; a stack trace will be printed unless the exception is SystemExit." ilk="function" name="start_new_thread" signature="start_new_thread(function, args[, kwargs])(start_new() is an obsolete synonym)  Start a new thread and return its identifier.  The thread will call the function with positional arguments from the tuple args and keyword arguments taken from the optional dictionary kwargs.  The thread exits when the function returns; the return value is ignored.  The thread will also exit when the function raises an unhandled exception; a stack trace will be printed unless the exception is SystemExit." />
