      <scope doc="Start a file with its associatedapplication.  When&#10;&quot;operation&quot; is not specified or &quot;open&quot;, this acts like&#10;double-clicking the file in Explorer, or giving the file&#10;name as an argument to the DOS &quot;start&quot; command: the file is&#10;opened with whatever application (if any) its extension is&#10;associated. When another &quot;operation&quot; is given, it specifies&#10;what should be done with the file.  A typical operation is&#10;&quot;print&quot;.  startfile returns as soon as the associated&#10;application is launched." ilk="function" name="startfile" signature="startfile(filepath [, operation])" />
