    <scope doc="(Ostensibly) fix copyright notices in files.&#10;Actually, this sript will simply replace a block of text in a file from one string to another.  It will only do this once though, i.e. not globally throughout the file.  It writes a backup file and then does an os.rename() dance for atomicity.  Usage: fixnotices.py [options] [filenames] Options: -h / --help Print this message and exit " ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Tools.Scripts.fixnotice">
