    <scope doc="JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) &lt;http://json.org&gt; is a subset ofJavaScript syntax (ECMA-262 3rd edition) used as a lightweight data interchange format.  :mod:`json` exposes an API familiar to users of the standard library :mod:`marshal` and :mod:`pickle` modules. It is the externally maintained version of the :mod:`json` library contained in Python 2.6, but maintains compatibility with Python 2.4 and Python 2.5 and (currently) has significant performance advantages, even without using the optional C extension for speedups. " ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Lib.json">
