    <scope doc="Switchboard class.&#10;This class is used to coordinate updates among all Viewers.  Every Viewer must conform to the following interface:  - it must include a method called update_yourself() which takes three arguments; the red, green, and blue values of the selected color.  - When a Viewer selects a color and wishes to update all other Views, it should call update_views() on the Switchboard object.  Note that the Viewer typically does *not* update itself before calling update_views(), since this would cause it to get updated twice." ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Tools.pynche.Switchboard">
