      <scope classrefs="DocTestRunner" doc="Run doc tests but raise an exception as soon as there is a failure.&#10;If an unexpected exception occurs, an UnexpectedException is raised. It contains the test, the example, and the original exception:  &gt;&gt;&gt; runner = DebugRunner(verbose=False) &gt;&gt;&gt; test = DocTestParser().get_doctest('&gt;&gt;&gt; raise KeyError\n42', ...                                    {}, 'foo', 'foo.py', 0) &gt;&gt;&gt; try: ...     runner.run(test) ... except UnexpectedException as f: ...     failure = f" ilk="class" line="1702" lineend="1803" name="DebugRunner">
