      <scope classrefs="object" doc="Unpickler(file, *, encoding='ASCII', errors='strict')This takes a binary file for reading a pickle data stream.  The protocol version of the pickle is detected automatically, so no proto argument is needed.  The file-like object must have two methods, a read() method that takes an integer argument, and a readline() method that requires no arguments.  Both methods should return bytes. Thus file-like object can be a binary file object opened for reading, a BytesIO object, or any other custom object that" ilk="class" name="Unpickler">
