    <scope doc="Turtle graphics is a popular way for introducing programming tokids. It was part of the original Logo programming language developed by Wally Feurzig and Seymour Papert in 1966.  Imagine a robotic turtle starting at (0, 0) in the x-y plane. After an ``import turtle``, give it the command turtle.forward(15), and it moves (on-screen!) 15 pixels in the direction it is facing, drawing a line as it moves. Give it the command turtle.right(25), and it rotates in-place 25 degrees clockwise.  By combining together these and similar commands, intricate shapes and pictures can easily be drawn." ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Lib.turtle">
      <scope classrefs="Widget XView YView" doc="Canvas widget to display graphical elements like lines or text." ilk="class" line="454" name="Canvas">
        <scope doc="Delete tag or id given as last arguments in ARGS from&#10;itemsidentified by first argument in ARGS." ilk="function" name="dtag" signature="dtag(self, *args)" />
