        <scope doc="Return a string describing the class of the operand.The&#10;returned value is one of the following ten strings:  *&#10;'-Infinity', indicating that the operand is negative&#10;infinity. * '-Normal', indicating that the operand is a&#10;negative normal number. * '-Subnormal', indicating that the&#10;operand is negative and subnormal. * '-Zero', indicating&#10;that the operand is a negative zero. * '+Zero', indicating&#10;that the operand is a positive zero. * '+Subnormal',&#10;indicating that the operand is positive and subnormal. *&#10;'+Normal', indicating that the operand is a positive normal&#10;number. * '+Infinity', indicating that the operand is&#10;positive infinity." ilk="function" name="number_class" signature="number_class([context])" />
