    <scope doc="Heap queue algorithm (a.k.a. priority queue).&#10;Heaps are arrays for which a[k] &lt;= a[2*k+1] and a[k] &lt;= a[2*k+2] for all k, counting elements from 0.  For the sake of comparison, non-existing elements are considered to be infinite.  The interesting property of a heap is that a[0] is always its smallest element.  Usage:  heap = []            # creates an empty heap heappush(heap, item) # pushes a new item on the heap item = heappop(heap) # pops the smallest item from the heap" ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="_heapq">
      <variable citdl="str" name="__about__" />
