      <scope classrefs="_TextIOBase" doc="Character and line based layer over a BufferedIOBase object, buffer.&#10;encoding gives the name of the encoding that the stream will be decoded or encoded with. It defaults to locale.getpreferredencoding(False).  errors determines the strictness of encoding and decoding (see the codecs.register) and defaults to &quot;strict&quot;.  newline can be None, '', '\n', '\r', or '\r\n'.  It controls the handling of line endings. If it is None, universal newlines is enabled.  With this enabled, on input, the lines endings '\n', '\r', or '\r\n' are translated to '\n' before being returned to the" ilk="class" name="TextIOWrapper">
