    <scope doc="finddiv - a grep-like tool that looks for division operators.&#10;Usage: finddiv [-l] file_or_directory ...  For directory arguments, all files in the directory whose name ends in .py are processed, and subdirectories are processed recursively.  This actually tokenizes the files to avoid false hits in comments or strings literals.  By default, this prints all lines containing a / or /= operator, in grep -n style.  With the -l option specified, it prints the filename" ilk="blob" lang="Python3" name="Tools.Scripts.finddiv">
