      <scope classrefs="object" doc="The core of the Distutils.  Most of the work hiding behind 'setup'is really done within a Distribution instance, which farms the work out to the Distutils commands specified on the command line.  Setup scripts will almost never instantiate Distribution directly, unless the 'setup()' function is totally inadequate to their needs. However, it is conceivable that a setup script might wish to subclass Distribution for some specialized purpose, and then pass the subclass to 'setup()' as the 'distclass' keyword argument.  If so, it is necessary to respect the expectations that 'setup' has of Distribution. See the code for 'setup()', in core.py, for details." ilk="class" line="27" lineend="966" name="Distribution">
