      <scope doc="addr-spec = local-part &quot;@&quot; domain" ilk="function" name="get_addr_spec" signature="get_addr_spec(value)" />
      <scope doc="address = mailbox / group Note that counter-intuitively, an&#10;address can be either a single address or a list of&#10;addresses (a group)." ilk="function" name="get_address" signature="get_address(value)" />
      <scope doc="address_list = (address *(&quot;,&quot; address)) / obs-addr-listobs-&#10;addr-list = *([CFWS] &quot;,&quot;) address *(&quot;,&quot; [address / CFWS])&#10;We depart from the formal grammar here by continuing to&#10;parse until the end of the input, assuming the input to be&#10;entirely composed of an address-list. This is always true in&#10;email parsing, and allows us to skip invalid addresses to&#10;parse additional valid ones." ilk="function" name="get_address_list" signature="get_address_list(value)" />
      <scope doc="angle-addr = [CFWS] &quot;&lt;&quot; addr-spec &quot;&gt;&quot; [CFWS] / obs-angle-&#10;addrobs-angle-addr = [CFWS] &quot;&lt;&quot; obs-route addr-spec &quot;&gt;&quot;&#10;[CFWS]" ilk="function" name="get_angle_addr" signature="get_angle_addr(value)" />
      <scope doc="atext = &lt;matches _atext_matcher&gt; We allow any non-ATOM_ENDS&#10;in atext, but add an InvalidATextDefect to the token's&#10;defects list if we find non-atext characters." ilk="function" name="get_atext" signature="get_atext(value)" />
      <scope doc="atom = [CFWS] 1*atext [CFWS]" ilk="function" name="get_atom" signature="get_atom(value)" />
      <scope doc="[CFWS] 1*attrtext [CFWS] This version of the BNF makes the&#10;CFWS explicit, and as usual we use a value terminal for the&#10;actual run of characters." ilk="function" name="get_attribute" signature="get_attribute(value)" />
      <scope doc="attrtext = 1*(any non-ATTRIBUTE_ENDS character) We allow any&#10;non-ATTRIBUTE_ENDS in attrtext, but add defects to the&#10;token's defects list if we find non-attrtext characters." ilk="function" name="get_attrtext" signature="get_attrtext(value)" />
      <scope doc="bare-quoted-string = DQUOTE *([FWS] qcontent) [FWS] DQUOTE A&#10;quoted-string without the leading or trailing white space." ilk="function" name="get_bare_quoted_string" signature="get_bare_quoted_string(value)" />
      <scope doc="CFWS = (1*([FWS] comment) [FWS]) / FWS" ilk="function" name="get_cfws" signature="get_cfws(value)" />
      <scope doc="comment = &quot;(&quot; *([FWS] ccontent) [FWS] &quot;)&quot;ccontent = ctext /&#10;quoted-pair / comment  We handle nested comments here, and&#10;quoted-pair in our qp-ctext routine." ilk="function" name="get_comment" signature="get_comment(value)" />
      <scope doc="display-name = phrase Because this is simply a name-rule, we&#10;don't return a display-name token containing a phrase, but&#10;rather a display-name token with the content of the phrase." ilk="function" name="get_display_name" signature="get_display_name(value)" />
      <scope doc="domain = dot-atom / domain-literal / obs-domainobs-domain =&#10;atom *(&quot;.&quot; atom))" ilk="function" name="get_domain" signature="get_domain(value)" />
      <scope doc="domain-literal = [CFWS] &quot;[&quot; *([FWS] dtext) [FWS] &quot;]&quot; [CFWS]" ilk="function" name="get_domain_literal" signature="get_domain_literal(value)" />
      <scope doc="dot-atom = [CFWS] dot-atom-text [CFWS]" ilk="function" name="get_dot_atom" signature="get_dot_atom(value)" />
      <scope doc="dot-text = 1*atext *(&quot;.&quot; 1*atext)" ilk="function" name="get_dot_atom_text" signature="get_dot_atom_text(value)" />
      <scope doc="dtext = &lt;printable ascii except \ [ ]&gt; / obs-dtextobs-dtext&#10;= obs-NO-WS-CTL / quoted-pair  We allow anything except the&#10;excluded characters, but but if we find any ASCII other than&#10;the RFC defined printable ASCII an NonPrintableDefect is&#10;added to the token's defects list. Quoted pairs are&#10;converted to their unquoted values, so what is returned is a&#10;ptext token, in this case a ValueTerminal." ilk="function" name="get_dtext" signature="get_dtext(value)" />
      <scope doc="encoded-word = &quot;=?&quot; charset &quot;?&quot; encoding &quot;?&quot; encoded-text&#10;&quot;?=&quot;" ilk="function" name="get_encoded_word" signature="get_encoded_word(value)" />
      <scope doc="[CFWS] 1*extended_attrtext [CFWS] This is like the non-&#10;extended version except we allow % characters, so that we&#10;can pick up an encoded value as a single string." ilk="function" name="get_extended_attribute" signature="get_extended_attribute(value)" />
      <scope doc="attrtext = 1*(any non-ATTRIBUTE_ENDS character plus '%')&#10;This is a special parsing routine so that we get a value&#10;that includes % escapes as a single string (which we decode&#10;as a single string later)." ilk="function" name="get_extended_attrtext" signature="get_extended_attrtext(value)" />
      <scope doc="FWS = 1*WSP This isn't the RFC definition." ilk="function" name="get_fws" signature="get_fws(value)" />
      <scope doc="group = display-name &quot;:&quot; [group-list] &quot;;&quot; [CFWS]" ilk="function" name="get_group" signature="get_group(value)" />
      <scope doc="group-list = mailbox-list / CFWS / obs-group-listobs-group-&#10;list = 1*([CFWS] &quot;,&quot;) [CFWS]" ilk="function" name="get_group_list" signature="get_group_list(value)" />
      <scope doc="Read everything up to one of the chars in endchars." ilk="function" name="get_invalid_mailbox" signature="get_invalid_mailbox(value, endchars)" />
      <scope doc="Read everything up to the next ';'." ilk="function" name="get_invalid_parameter" signature="get_invalid_parameter(value)" />
      <scope doc="local-part = dot-atom / quoted-string / obs-local-part" ilk="function" name="get_local_part" signature="get_local_part(value)" />
      <scope doc="mailbox = name-addr / addr-spec" ilk="function" name="get_mailbox" signature="get_mailbox(value)" />
      <scope doc="mailbox-list = (mailbox *(&quot;,&quot; mailbox)) / obs-mbox-listobs-&#10;mbox-list = *([CFWS] &quot;,&quot;) mailbox *(&quot;,&quot; [mailbox / CFWS])&#10;For this routine we go outside the formal grammar in order&#10;to improve error handling. We recognize the end of the&#10;mailbox list only at the end of the value or at a ';' (the&#10;group terminator)." ilk="function" name="get_mailbox_list" signature="get_mailbox_list(value)" />
      <scope doc="name-addr = [display-name] angle-addr" ilk="function" name="get_name_addr" signature="get_name_addr(value)" />
      <scope doc="obs-local-part = word *(&quot;.&quot; word)" ilk="function" name="get_obs_local_part" signature="get_obs_local_part(value)" />
      <scope doc="obs-route = obs-domain-list &quot;:&quot;obs-domain-list = *(CFWS /&#10;&quot;,&quot;) &quot;@&quot; domain *(&quot;,&quot; [CFWS] [&quot;@&quot; domain])  Returns an obs-&#10;route token with the appropriate sub-tokens (that is, there&#10;is no obs-domain-list in the parse tree)." ilk="function" name="get_obs_route" signature="get_obs_route(value)" />
      <scope doc="attribute [section] [&quot;*&quot;] [CFWS] &quot;=&quot; value The CFWS is&#10;implied by the RFC but not made explicit in the BNF." ilk="function" name="get_parameter" signature="get_parameter(value)" />
      <scope doc="phrase = 1*word / obs-phraseobs-phrase = word *(word / &quot;.&quot; /&#10;CFWS)  This means a phrase can be a sequence of words,&#10;periods, and CFWS in any order as long as it starts with at&#10;least one word. If anything other than words is detected, an&#10;ObsoleteHeaderDefect is added to the token's defect list." ilk="function" name="get_phrase" signature="get_phrase(value)" />
      <scope doc="qcontent = qtext / quoted-pair We allow anything except the&#10;DQUOTE character, but if we find any ASCII other than the&#10;RFC defined printable ASCII an NonPrintableDefect is added&#10;to the token's defects list." ilk="function" name="get_qcontent" signature="get_qcontent(value)" />
      <scope doc="ctext = &lt;printable ascii except \ ( )&gt; This is not the RFC&#10;ctext, since we are handling nested comments in comment and&#10;unquoting quoted-pairs here." ilk="function" name="get_qp_ctext" signature="get_qp_ctext(value)" />
      <scope doc="quoted-string = [CFWS] &lt;bare-quoted-string&gt; [CFWS] 'bare-&#10;quoted-string' is an intermediate class defined by this&#10;parser and not by the RFC grammar." ilk="function" name="get_quoted_string" signature="get_quoted_string(value)" />
      <scope doc="'*' digits The formal BNF is more complicated because&#10;leading 0s are not allowed." ilk="function" name="get_section" signature="get_section(value)" />
      <scope doc="token = [CFWS] 1*ttext [CFWS] The RFC equivalent of ttext is&#10;any US-ASCII chars except space, ctls, or tspecials." ilk="function" name="get_token" signature="get_token(value)" />
      <scope doc="ttext = &lt;matches _ttext_matcher&gt; We allow any non-TOKEN_ENDS&#10;in ttext, but add defects to the token's defects list if we&#10;find non-ttext characters." ilk="function" name="get_ttext" signature="get_ttext(value)" />
      <scope doc="unstructured = (*([FWS] vchar) *WSP) / obs-unstructobs-&#10;unstruct = *((*LF *CR *(obs-utext) *LF *CR)) / FWS) obs-&#10;utext = %d0 / obs-NO-WS-CTL / LF / CR  obs-NO-WS-CTL is&#10;control characters except WSP/CR/LF. So, basically, we have&#10;printable runs, plus control characters or nulls in the&#10;obsolete syntax, separated by whitespace." ilk="function" name="get_unstructured" signature="get_unstructured(value)" />
      <scope doc="quoted-string / attribute" ilk="function" name="get_value" signature="get_value(value)" />
      <scope doc="word = atom / quoted-string Either atom or quoted-string may&#10;start with CFWS." ilk="function" name="get_word" signature="get_word(value)" />
      <scope doc="Returns a new subclass of tuple with named fields." ilk="function" name="namedtuple" signature="namedtuple(typename, field_names, verbose=False, rename=False)" />
      <scope doc="disposition-type *( &quot;;&quot; parameter )" ilk="function" name="parse_content_disposition_header" signature="parse_content_disposition_header(value)" />
      <scope doc="mechanism" ilk="function" name="parse_content_transfer_encoding_header" signature="parse_content_transfer_encoding_header(value)" />
      <scope doc="maintype &quot;/&quot; subtype *( &quot;;&quot; parameter ) The maintype and&#10;substype are tokens." ilk="function" name="parse_content_type_header" signature="parse_content_type_header(value)" />
      <scope doc="parameter *( &quot;;&quot; parameter ) That BNF is meant to indicate&#10;this routine should only be called after finding and&#10;handling the leading ';'." ilk="function" name="parse_mime_parameters" signature="parse_mime_parameters(value)" />
      <scope doc="mime-version = [CFWS] 1*digit [CFWS] &quot;.&quot; [CFWS] 1*digit&#10;[CFWS]" ilk="function" name="parse_mime_version" signature="parse_mime_version(value)" />
